 "text": "Hey there! How's your day been so far? The turkey makes great sandwiches, but I' got some other ideas. How about chili con carne, or spaghetti with the turkey meat? No, day old rice works fine. Just leave it in the pantry instead of the fridge, it stays fresher. It' fine, just rinse it well. Then toss it with oil, some seasoning and water, and cook it until al dente. A chicken stock, a bit of soy sauce, some chopped cilantro. You could also add some frozen peas at the end for a little sweetness. Freeze it within four hours of cooking, or toss it. Then use it in the next week or so.",
